# QBusto — single ignore file for the whole repository.
#
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth, so one rule here covers
# backend/, consumer/, dashboard/ and kitchen/ alike. Per-application
# .gitignore files were removed in favour of this one; add new rules here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files
#
# Real configuration never enters the repository. The committed *.env.example
# files are not matched by these patterns and are the documented template.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.bak
*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.cache/
.vite/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local databases
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling and scratch work
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
scratchpad/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only developer scripts
#
# Kept on disk, never committed: this one writes real user rows with passwords
# chosen on the command line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/scripts/create-dev-user.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal engineering documentation
#
# Excluded from the repository by request. These stay on disk for the
# development team but are not part of what is handed over.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/docs/pos-integration.md
backend/docs/backend-verification.md
backend/docs/development-guide.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded images
#
# Files staff upload through the Dashboard are user data, not source. They live
# under the directory named by FILE_STORAGE_PATH, which defaults to
# `shared/uploads` - the same shared directory that holds the generated
# openapi.json. Only the uploads subtree is ignored; shared/openapi.json is
# committed and stays committed.
#
# These files belong in the server's backups, never in git. On a production
# server FILE_STORAGE_PATH is normally an absolute path outside the source
# tree, in which case this rule is simply inert.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
shared/uploads/
